---
import H from "@/components/H.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
import StatGrid from "@/components/StatGrid.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="FRC 12148"
    description="Team V.A.N. is a student-led FIRST Robotics Competition team in Palm Bay, Florida, serving students in southern Brevard and Indian River counties."
>
    <H class="mb-4">Team V.A.N.</H>

    <p>
        Team V.A.N. is a student-led FIRST Robotics Competition team based in
        Palm Bay. Our students design, build, and program competition robots,
        and they also take on sponsorships, fundraising, outreach, and the
        design decisions that shape the season.
    </p>

    <Section aria-labelledby="what-is-frc-heading">
        <H id="what-is-frc-heading" level="h2">
            What is FIRST Robotics?
        </H>
        <p>
            The FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) is an international high school
            engineering program. Every January, teams get a Kit of Parts and a
            new game, then have about six weeks to design, build, program, and
            test a competition robot before shipping it off to events. From
            February through April, teams compete in head-to-head matches at
            regional and district events around the world, working to qualify
            for the FIRST Championship.
        </p>
        <p>
            FRC runs on two values as much as it runs on robots:{" "}
            <strong>Gracious Professionalism</strong>, treating competitors with
            the same respect as teammates, and <strong>Coopertition</strong>,
            the idea that teams can help each other and still compete hard.
            Teams also earn judged awards for engineering quality, community
            impact, and mentorship, not just match wins.
        </p>
        <StatGrid
            stats={[
                { value: "3,700+", label: "teams worldwide" },
                { value: "33", label: "countries & regions" },
                { value: "90,000+", label: "students competing" },
                { value: "~600", label: "teams at FIRST Championship" },
            ]}
        />
    </Section>

    <Section>
        <H level="h2">What we do</H>
        <p>
            Founded in 2026, Team V.A.N. (FRC 12148) is in its first FRC season.
            Students run the technical work and the day-to-day organization of
            the team, with four leads managing organization and business. How
            those roles are split, and where we meet and build, is on the{" "}
            <a
                href="/about/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                About
            </a>{" "}
            page.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our main build space is in Palm Bay, near Palm Bay Magnet, Bayside
            High, and Heritage High. We are also the closest FRC team to
            Sebastian River High, Vero Beach High, and Indian River Charter
            High.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Why this team exists</H>
        <p>
            We started the team because southern Brevard County and Indian River
            County have had limited access to FRC. Indian River County currently
            has no FRC teams, and students in southern Brevard often have to
            travel a long way to join an existing program.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">This season</H>
        <p>
            We expect about 15 students and hope to recruit 15 to 20 committed
            members. We plan to compete at the Orlando Regional and the Rocket
            City Regional, and at the FIRST Championship if we qualify.
            Competition dates and venues are on the{" "}
            <a
                href="/competitions/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                Competitions
            </a>{" "}
            page.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Sponsorship</H>
        <p>
            As a first-year team we are still putting operations, travel,
            registration, and a robot in place at the same time. Sponsor support
            helps cover those operating costs, and sponsors are featured on team
            shirts and the website. Details are on the{" "}
            <a
                href="/sponsors/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                Sponsors
            </a>{" "}
            page.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Join us</H>
        <p>
            Students interested in building, programming or business are
            welcome. Anyone can join, regardless of experience.{" "}
            <a
                href="/interest/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                Fill out the interest form
            </a>
            .
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Want to help?</H>
        <p>
            If you are in the area and would like to support the team, you can
            reach us at{" "}
            <a
                href="mailto:contact@teamvan.org"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                contact@teamvan.org
            </a>
            .
        </p>
    </Section>
</Layout>
